course: dictionary
lesson: 2182
title: Cos: a short word for because
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: In casual talk, people often shorten words. Cos is a short, spoken form of because, and you may also see it written as 'cause or coz. «I'm late cos the bus broke down.» The words after cos give the reason, so cos means because here.
explain: Test it by swapping the word. Put because in place of cos: «I'm late because the bus broke down.» If the sentence still makes sense and keeps the same meaning, you have found the right word. Chloe from Belfast says, «Cos I'm Irish, so I am,» which means "Because I'm Irish, I am", so cos gives a reason.
explain: Cos is for speaking and casual writing, like texts with friends. In school writing, use because. Older pupils may also meet cos in maths, where it is short for cosine and is written next to an angle, like cos 60°. That is a different meaning, so check which subject you are reading.
fact: Cos is a short, informal spoken form of because.
fact: You may also see it written as 'cause or coz.
fact: In «I'm late cos the bus broke down», cos introduces the reason.
fact: Cos is not used in formal writing, so write because in school essays and letters.
fact: In maths, cos is short for cosine, a function used with angles in triangles, as in cos 60°.
exercise: «I'm late cos the bus broke down.» What does cos mean here? | Before | Although | Until | *Because
exercise: Chloe says, «Cos I'm Irish, so I am.» What is cos doing in her sentence? | *Giving a reason | Asking a question | Saying goodbye | Naming a country
exercise: You are writing a school essay. Which word should you use instead of cos? | 'cause | cos | *because | coz
test: Ella says, «I'm late cos I missed the bus.» Which word could replace cos without changing the meaning? | Although | *Because | While | After
test: In maths, cos 60° is short for what? | A cousin | *Cosine | A coat | A cost
exam: Which word means the same as cos in «We stayed in cos it rained»? | Until | *Because | Unless | Although
